 if  he can survive holding his companions  above his head  safe from their boiling oil face for one  hour they can go free  and the crazy part is he does it  for one full hour his body is cooked by  the boiling  oil around him all the while holding his  friends above a grim  grim death easily the most heroic story  of the series for me  and one that shook me to my very core  when i read what happened next  knowing full well that he will last a  full hour at the last minute orochi  changes the sentence to death  by firing squad and with that odin  launches his friends into the sky  telling them to flee and to open oneo's  borders  and with that they dash into the  distance now driven by new purpose  odin however he wasn't so lucky shot by  kaido between the eyes his last words  being  build your strength while you can for i  am a story to accompany your drinks  this heinous and cruel action saddens  everyone deeply but sends denjiro  into an intense rage that contorts his  face leading him to go by kyoshiro  the mad thereafter in the following  chapter we then finally get a chance to  see how the events of lady taki and the  samurai got thrust into the future with  momonosuke and how hiyori found herself  to be where she ultimately ended up  thanks to the helping hand of kyoshiro  these flashback sequences were a breath  of fresh air and some of my favorite  moments from the entire series i think  it should go without saying that this  large flashback is the single best  flashback sequence from the entire story  bar none introducing us to a brilliant  and lovable character in odin as he  gains friendship  a sense of duty maturity and family all  the while traveling across the world in  search of adventure but the next  sequence of events  brought such an overwhelming flood of  emotion to the surface for me i simply  had to dedicate this portion of the  video to chapters 9 7  4 and 9 7 5. effectively the last 18  chapters and  well really the last few acts have been  building at least in part  to this moment the moment where the  rebellion they had all fought so  fiercely to keep hope alive for  and no one is here as an audience we are  now armed with the experiences of  all the loyal followers ready to lay  down their lives  my heart felt heavy and sunken as i  watched these poor broken men and women  stand before the roaring  fierce angry seas totally utterly alone  after all the hard work they had put  into bringing this planet into action  surrounded by destruction they suspect  that once again the word must have  gotten back to orochi concerning the new  plan  and where it was taking place getting  aboard this tiny boat setting towards  certain doom  they come to understand that it must be  one of them and then  this happens  this single panel sends shivers down my  spine the likes of which i don't think  i'll ever forget and it makes perfect  sense going all the way back to when we  first met up with kenduro in dressrosa  of all the samurai they met along the  way  all who cried upon seeing each other  kanjuro was the only one not to show any  emotion  and the first thing he asks is about  momonosuke's status  what's more is that dotted throughout  this vast story are panels that give  hints to this character being the bad  guy  all along and that's honestly what i  love to see in storytelling  after he reveals who he truly is a  member of the same kurozumi clan  orochi's part of kaido's massive  warships begin steamrolling forward  towards their small dinghy enraged by  this news kinemon slices off kenjuro's  head  but it's not him it's a perfect copy but  kanjuro could never really draw that  well well this  is about where i had it points out to me  that he had all this time  been using his non-dominant hand to draw  everything and at every turn  tried to prevent progress and  furthermore he was the one that led  kaido's forces to zou in the first place  at this point i was totally and  completely floored by the competence of  this swerve  never in all of my life have i ever  experienced a story swerve  exactly how the author intended me to so  perfectly  this chapter captured my imagination  like none other in this series and  brought every single shred of hope  crashing down to the lowest they have  ever been in the series and now that oda  has taken us to as low as he can  possibly go  now is the time to inject hope back into  the series  suddenly out of nowhere cannons from  three vessels meet their mark on kaido's  monstrous ships  finally breaking the cycle of despair  seeing him for the very first time in so  many  chapters stands luffy pictured alongside  law and kid  ready to take on kaido in the span of 17  pages oda had me crying tears of sadness  and utter relief what an outstandingly  brilliant storyteller  and it's not over yet in the next  chapter oda raises our spirits again  again  as orochi and kaido ready for the  festivities on the island luffy  kid and law attacked their battleships  and to make matters even better  kyoshiro is now here revealing that he  is in fact dengiro  to everybody much to the dismay of the  traitor he sought to outsmart  and outsmart but the true gigabrain play  of the entire rebellion has to be from  kinaemon  convincing the traitor that the  rebellion was taking place on the tokage  port  and not the wharf even hiding numbers  from kanjiro that proved to be crucial  in the closing moments of this encounter  my mind man my mind is fried in the most  beautiful way  kinemon with the galaxy brain play that  saved  the day  i honestly don't think i've ever been  more happy reading a story in  all of my life sincerely a  heart-wrenching heartbreaking  breathtaking uplifting and harrowing  moment  that sends shivers to my very core wano  is  easily the best arc in one piece for me  like i know it's not even done yet but  even if all oda did was print 2.5 more  acts of blank pages  this would still be better than anything  he's ever done in my opinion and while  this  isn't the end of where the manga is  currently right now  i think it's where i'm gonna end my  review while also offering and  encouraging anyone who can't wait for my  next review of one piece to drop to  instead pick up this incredible story  and read through it for yourselves this  really is a tale that deserves to be  supported  and experienced first hand over the last  half a year i've dedicated myself to  catching up to the one piece story  and to document it as authentically as i  can to give you all my blind review of  this wonderful series that's captured  the hearts of millions young and old  throughout the world i think it goes  without saying that this experience has  exceeded any and all high expectations i  had before entering into this  self-imposed challenge  and this quite simply couldn't have been  done without my incredible editor  or my one piece team backing me up the  entire way i'll never be able to grow up  with this series like i did with dragon  ball  but during the time i wrote and reviewed  this incredible tale of heisi's  adventure  i've moved into my first home gotten  engaged and gained a new family member  so i guess i can say that one piece has  been there for some of the most  important moments of my life i can't  wait to continue this story with you all  but  until then as always i've been totally  not mark  and thank you so much for watching  why didn't no one tell me that this  story was like the best thing ever  but you'd be surprised how if i didn't  already love zorro's character this  would be the moment i'd propose to him  i might have fallen in love with him  there and then  piece of verve or life paper  [Music]  this wasn't the best arc so far  if a lot of people love each other the  world would be a better place to live  [Music]  you
 

